#!/usr/bin/env bash
# flow176 (2026-09-10, WIN-FIRST GATE arm): the deployed flow168 recipe, byte for byte, with the gate's verdict swapped from `leg20` to the campaign's own promotion rule. Same tree, same theta layout, same 56-board held-out live set, same 103-opponent field; only the gate's rule and the run/seed/GPU differ. Verbatim provenance: ssh user@remote-host 'cat ~/launch_flow168.sh', fetched 2026-09-10 (22,700 bytes).
# WHY: on 2026-09-10 flow168's leg20 gate REFUSED a candidate that took the held-out live set from 98 wins to 108 (+14 flips / -4 drops) because the family paired coin delta read -608 a game. The local judge promotes WIN RATE FIRST -- the win count rises with few drops and the margin is not down -- so the gate's verdict was the opposite of the rule the record is kept on. `--real-gate-metric winfirst` reads the SAME family on the SAME rows and makes the count the verdict, with the coin delta as a bounded price.
# CHANGES vs the deployed flow168, exactly six: (1) the metric becomes winfirst; (2) min-flips 3 -> 6 -- and under winfirst that flag is read again in a DIFFERENT UNIT, it counts BOARDS not games (a pinned town replays the identical game in either seat, so the 112 family games are 56 boards, and 6 net boards is the +14/-4 candidate's shape rather than its double); (3) NEW --real-gate-margin-slack 800, the coins a family game the flips may cost -- the family AND all-games paired deltas must each be >= -800 a game, so flow168's -608 passes and a -12k collapse does not; (4) --run flow176; (5) --seed 276; (6) CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 (sed it to the free GPU before launching). Everything else -- init theta, sigma 0.015, --tape-actions, every --rung-weight, --real-gate-opponent, --real-gate-leg-family (the 56 held-out tapes), --real-gate-pinned-seats 2, --real-gate-every 100, --real-gate-recentre 3 -- is unchanged.
# STAGE: this arm is a CODE change (src/kagg3/es/train.py + scripts/train.py carry the new metric). rsync this worktree's src/ scripts/ tests/ over ~/stage_draingene BEFORE launching, or scripts/train.py refuses the metric at argparse -- which is the failure we want rather than a silent fallback.
# LAUNCH: sed -i "s/__GPU__/N/g" ~/launch_flow176.sh && nohup bash ~/launch_flow176.sh &
set -euo pipefail
cd ~/stage_draingene
mkdir -p artifacts/flow176
source ~/kagg3/.venv/bin/activate
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python scripts/train.py \
  --run flow176 \
  --init-theta artifacts/kagg2_games/thetas/flow166_g170_gd.npy --weight-decay 0 --sigma 0.015 \
  --stall-sigma-mult 1.0 --best-replicate 2 --abs-select all --best-margin 0.04 \
  --select-metric score --abs-weight 0.0 --margin-scale 3000 --train-only all --d10-cash-weight 0 --tile-fill-weight 0 --fitness-manifest \
